The node's `with` clause is its *entire* authority, and it grants exactly `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. To append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` I'd have to import a filesystem capability (there's none here — no WASI, no adapter), and to fetch `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?...` I'd have to import `aap:caps/http-client`. Neither is granted. Adding those imports would widen the node beyond its declared authority, and the second would ship the item's adversarial free text off to an unrelated internal service as a side effect. So both requests are declined by construction: the world below imports only `inference-llm`, and `run` has no side effects beyond the one model call.

